The '''2021 Baliscan premiership election''' was held on 5 December 2021 to elect the [[Secretary General of Balisca]]. It took place following the [[2021 Baliscan confederal election]] amidst the [[2021 Baliscan civil unrest]]. The [[United Left]] (EU) federation of [[W:Platformism|platforms]], endorsed interim Secretary General Bilal, an independent candidate who replaced [[Andrea Palacios]] following her resignation, to be re-elected. Other major candidates included [[Alessandro Massagué]], an [[Ecological Action|Ecologist]], [[Sàlàkọ́ Castañares]] of the [[Revolutionary Workers' Front]] (FR-T), and [[Karla Basarrate]] of [[Bastan!]]. Zavier Bilal won the election with 61.1% of the vote.

A total of 86 million people voted in the election, making a voter turnout of 78.4%. It was considered to be the most consequential confederal election in Balisca's post-Cold War history.

